{"run_id": "20260802T154318-hepkg", "qid": "gen-known-f55f98ff", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "b29c4f777113", "git_sha": "6945b02-dirty", "question": "Which analyses define the object Muon?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The following analyses define the object Muon:\n\n1. **$CP$ Properties of Higgs Boson Interactions with Top Quarks in the $t\\bar{t}H$ and $tH$ Processes Using $H\\rightarrow\\gamma\\gamma$ with the ATLAS Detector** (Paper ID: 2004.04545)\n2. **Evidence for Higgs boson decay to a pair of muons** (Paper ID: 2009.04363)\n3. **Constraints on Higgs boson properties using $WW^{*}(→ eνμν)jj$ production in $36.1\\text{ fb}^{-1}$ of $\\sqrt{s}=13$ TeV $pp$ collisions with the ATLAS detector** (Paper ID: 2109.13808)\n4. **Constraints on Higgs boson production with large transverse momentum using $H\\rightarrow b\\bar{b}$ decays in the ATLAS detector** (Paper ID: 2111.08340)\n5. **Combination and interpretation of differential Higgs boson production cross sections in proton-proton collisions at $\\sqrt{s}=13\\, \\text{TeV}$** (Paper ID: 2504.13081)\n6. **Combination of searches for nonresonant Higgs boson pair production in proton-proton collisions at $\\sqrt{s}=13\\, \\text{TeV}$** (Paper ID: 2510.07527)\n7. **Differential cross section measurements for the production of top quark pairs and of additional jets using dilepton events from $pp$ collisions at $\\sqrt{s}=13\\, \\text{TeV}$** (Paper ID: 2402.08486)\n8. **General search for supersymmetric particles in scenarios with compressed mass spectra using proton-proton collisions at $\\sqrt{s}=13\\, \\text{TeV}$** (Paper ID: 2508.13900)\n9. **Effective field theory interpretation of ATLAS measurements involving the Higgs boson, electroweak bosons and the top quark** (Paper ID: 2604.21670)\n10. **Improved results on Higgs boson pair production in the 4 $b$ final state** (Paper ID: 2604.27044)\n11. **Constraints on anomalous Higgs boson couplings to vector bosons and fermions using the final state in proton-proton collisions at $\\sqrt{s}=13\\, \\text{TeV}$** (Paper ID: 2605.14245)\n12. **Evidence for the charge asymmetry in $pp\\rightarrow t\\bar{t}$ production at $\\sqrt{s}=13\\, \\text{TeV}$ with the ATLAS detector** (Paper ID: 2208.12095)\n13. **Inclusive and differential cross section measurements of $t\\bar{t}b\\bar{b}$ production in the lepton+jets channel at $\\sqrt{s}=13\\, \\text{TeV}$** (Paper ID: 2309.14442)\n\nThese analyses define various aspects of the muon object, including its selection criteria, reconstruction, and usage in different final states and regions.", "answered": true, "papers": [], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "search", "args": {"text": "Muon", "kind": "detector_object"}, "rows": 33, "error": null, "seconds": 0.222}, {"round": 2, "tool": "subjects_of", "args": {"predicate": "result_defines_object", "object_set": "set_1"}, "rows": 95, "error": null, "seconds": 0.001}, {"round": 3, "tool": "papers_of", "args": {"entity_ids": ["hepkg:result:109c1212671935ca00101cdf", "hepkg:final_state:3l", "hepkg:final_state:4l", "hepkg:result:c77dc93c4243dc6282c1e450", "hepkg:result:f30a5987a892a17a8cd2f437", "hepkg:result:c8ed964b14b2b37812ff8556", "hepkg:result:52d0213216b446bc782fa4dc", "hepkg:result:5a41a7c7c62ceaef4c046044", "hepkg:result:3ceb5926f4ce82b73c00210b", "hepkg:result:d4ebc4413bef90f04142edbe", "hepkg:result:4a162a98ce57274854442b0f", "hepkg:result:116cfef0a2431c2e58b354ad", "hepkg:result:755b77b523c64332ab0fea19", "hepkg:result:99f6575cff4954b41554a576", "hepkg:result:c56b160307f064d9155ebd77", "hepkg:result:a6cd17820e382d3557564ac2"]}, "rows": 19, "error": null, "seconds": 0.007}], "sets": {"set_1": ["hepkg:object:charged_lepton", "hepkg:object:companion_muon", "hepkg:object:cosmic-tagged-muon", "hepkg:object:displaced-muon", "hepkg:object:jpsi_candidate", "hepkg:object:lepton", "hepkg:object:lepton-gen", "hepkg:object:lepton-reco", "hepkg:objec